# --- data & artifacts ---
# Source data is never committed: it comes from `make data && make panel`,
# so the pipeline stays reproducible from source rather than from a blob
# checked in here. That rule still holds for everything under data/.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
!data/raw/
!data/interim/
!data/processed/
data/raw/*
data/interim/*
data/processed/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/interim/.gitkeep
!data/processed/.gitkeep

artifacts/*
!artifacts/.gitkeep

# DELIBERATE EXCEPTION -- the dashboard artifacts are committed.
#
# The hosted demo (Streamlit Community Cloud) clones this repo and has no
# way to run `make data` for itself: the real panel needs ~234 WER PDFs
# downloaded and parsed plus a rate-limited Open-Meteo backfill, which takes
# far longer than a cold start allows and would redo itself on every reboot.
# Without these files the public deployment can only ever show the synthetic
# demo panel, which undersells a platform whose whole point is real figures.
#
# What this does and does not relax:
#   * These are aggregate district-week counts from the Epidemiology Unit's
#     PUBLISHED Weekly Epidemiological Reports -- public, non-personal data.
#   * Source data (data/) stays ignored. The panel is still built from
#     source, not from anything committed here.
#   * Only the 14 files app/streamlit_app.py's ARTIFACT_NAMES actually reads
#     are listed. predictions.parquet (the largest, ~207 KB) is read by no
#     page and stays ignored.
#
# These are a dated SNAPSHOT, not live data. Refresh with
# `make data && make panel && make pipeline-real` and re-commit; the app
# shows the pipeline run time and panel date range on every page so a stale
# snapshot is visible as stale rather than passing as current.
!artifacts/pipeline_meta.parquet
!artifacts/district_risk.parquet
!artifacts/panel_recent.parquet
!artifacts/forecasts.parquet
!artifacts/scores.parquet
!artifacts/effect_table.parquet
!artifacts/allocation_sweep.parquet
!artifacts/allocation_summary.parquet
!artifacts/sei_sir_params.parquet
!artifacts/hospital_readiness.parquet
!artifacts/district_capacity.parquet
!artifacts/health_facilities.parquet
!artifacts/scenarios.parquet
!artifacts/budget_sweep.parquet

